        "raw-wiktextract-data.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "f11c1959-119d-31d3-852f-661f497b178f",
                "word": "Simonian",
                "pos": "adj",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "66f0a078-2471-4241-9d48-e8fdba27dc91",
                        "entry_id": "f11c1959-119d-31d3-852f-661f497b178f",
                        "tags": [
                            "comparative"
                        ],
                        "form": "more Simonian"
                    },
                    {
                        "form_id": "debf7680-cb12-4cf8-9276-e4dbb0680035",
                        "entry_id": "f11c1959-119d-31d3-852f-661f497b178f",
                        "tags": [
                            "superlative"
                        ],
                        "form": "most Simonian"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ba12023d-20af-30c8-81c1-9fb9925f2e53",
                        "entry_id": "f11c1959-119d-31d3-852f-661f497b178f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pertaining to the legends surrounding and teachings of Simon Magus."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "487c8287-c879-4422-aa20-495b49ab50d9",
                                "sense_id": "ba12023d-20af-30c8-81c1-9fb9925f2e53",
                                "text": "The Justin account is the nucleus of the huge Simonian legend which was mainly developed by the cycle of Pseudo-Clemenine literature of the third century, based on the second century Circuits of Peter."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a2580d2f-9eeb-4160-9be1-6b953c258315",
                                "sense_id": "ba12023d-20af-30c8-81c1-9fb9925f2e53",
                                "text": "If we agree that HSim was not a forgery, it remains to ask whether it is actually Simonian. For this question the identity and teachings of the historical Simon Magus — in any case irrecoverable —are not important."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "35ff59fd-ac6d-4095-a44d-d9281dbef02b",
                                "sense_id": "ba12023d-20af-30c8-81c1-9fb9925f2e53",
                                "text": "The amalgam of paganism and Christianity, especially obvious in the Simonian system , is readily explicable in the teachings of Simon Magus."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3c66d830-33fd-3ea6-81b7-7c6c91b071fc",
                        "entry_id": "f11c1959-119d-31d3-852f-661f497b178f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pertaining to the heretical sect that worshiped Simon of Samaria (Simon Magus)."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c73a54f5-b126-48fb-85f4-2936d6291cdf",
                                "sense_id": "3c66d830-33fd-3ea6-81b7-7c6c91b071fc",
                                "text": "Yet it must be acknowledg'd, that although a Pagan-like Mundane Magistracy of the Holy Angels was entertain'd by several of the Learned Theologers of the three first Ages of the Church, yet no such thang as Church-Demonolatry appeareth in those early Days, save only amongst the Simonian Gnosticks and the ancient Angelici or Angelits condemn'd by S Paul (Col. 2.18), which I suppose to have been a distinct sort of Gnosticks from the Simonian, who had their origin from Simon Magus."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b89ef2f7-4447-4eaa-b78c-2839408accff",
                                "sense_id": "3c66d830-33fd-3ea6-81b7-7c6c91b071fc",
                                "text": "Luke's choice of words appear to be subtle but also sharp and effective critiques of Simonian claims to Simon's divity."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "c71d3939-3644-4e44-a9f9-0c0df050027c",
                                "sense_id": "3c66d830-33fd-3ea6-81b7-7c6c91b071fc",
                                "text": "He considered the Simonian veneration of Simon to be blasphemy. He never seems to have examined why Simonians honored Simon's reputed icon."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "9491c43a-f0eb-3772-83bd-ea3c08e75c06",
                        "entry_id": "f11c1959-119d-31d3-852f-661f497b178f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Pertaining to the theories of Herbert A. Simon."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "1fdcdfd9-c155-4a23-822a-dd81564ec258",
                                "sense_id": "9491c43a-f0eb-3772-83bd-ea3c08e75c06",
                                "text": "Suppose you are a serious Christian and you come to recognize that Simonian science endorses conclusions incompatible with certain Christian beliefs; and suppose you also hold science in high regard."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "05a327bc-6716-400e-a585-b0a61319362b",
                                "sense_id": "9491c43a-f0eb-3772-83bd-ea3c08e75c06",
                                "text": "On the other hand, Simonian entrepreneurs are non-alert individuals who search for alternatives that are good enough for them."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3c6c4a54-da39-4a3d-8939-452623f352ba",
                                "sense_id": "9491c43a-f0eb-3772-83bd-ea3c08e75c06",
                                "text": "The result is a prism providing a spectrum of Simon's work and offering the reader a glimpse into how their own ideas can be seen through a Simonian lens."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [],
                "word_linkages": []
            },
